  "bio": [
    "Hemant Taneja now styles $43 billion venture fund General Catalyst as a \"global investment and transformation firm.\"",
    "Taneja's General Catalyst teamed up with billionaire activist investor Nelson Peltz last year to mount a $7.4 billion takeover offer for listed mutual fund giant Janus Henderson, which manages over $493 billion in assets.",
    "An early backer of Stripe, Snap, Anduril, Grammarly and Gusto, Taneja also plays a big role in the firm's health investments, including cofounding companies like Livongo (acquired by Teladoc Health for $18.5 billion in 2020).",
    "Since joining GC in 2001 and becoming CEO in 2021, Taneja led the firm's expansion efforts, including the launch of its West Coast office in 2010, its expansion into wealth management, buyouts and the takeover offer for Ohio hospital group Summa Health.",
    "Born in Delhi, Taneja immigrated to the U.S. at age 15.",
    "He sold his first company, wireless app maker Isovia to JP Mobile after dropping out of his MIT PhD program."
